/-
# Contour data for the I3 saddle certificate (PROOF_BETA §6.3, instance I3)

Rational vertices of the steepest-descent contour of `h = Re f`, `f = Ψ - 2πi x`:
* the upper polyline `upStart, upPts` from (the rounding of) `x₀ + ρ d` to
  `xtop ≈ 9.2117 + 60.012 i`,
  split into chunks `upC1 … upC5` so that their kernel checks live in separate files
  (`UpChunk1.lean` … `UpChunk5.lean`);
* the lower polyline `dnStart, dnPts` from (the rounding of) `x₀ - ρ d` down to the real point
  `x_c ≈ 1.161976 < 7/6`.

Generated by an RK4 trace of the steepest-descent ODE from `x₀ ± ρ d` (`ρ = 1/250`, seed
`x₀ ≈ 1.1718 + 0.00986 i`, as in the independent Python saddle certificate `d33_saddle_cert.py`), rounded to `10⁻¹²` and
simplified greedily against a float model of the Lean checks; every claim is re-checked by
`decide +kernel` in the files that use this data.

Constants: far threshold `T0 = -29.78` (`Re Ω ≈ -29.7790173`, so the far margin is `≈ 9.8·10⁻⁴`),
sector constants `amin = 1/1000`, `Amax = 2.76` (`η = π - 2.76 > 0.38`).

Status: complete (no `sorry`).
-/
